Part of #161

Portable, project-agnostic scripts the skill calls:
- check and install Blender's Python module (`bpy`) for the Python version it needs;
- render any `.fbx` / `.glb` / `.blend` from three-quarter, front, side and wireframe (Cycles on CPU, no GPU needed);
- compose a review sheet: concept on the left, renders on the right, a caption with the numbers.

**Done when:** each script runs on a model it has never seen (tested on a PlunderSpell model) and its output has been opened and looked at.
